From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 04:39:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Second look on Sonnet for hard inbox drafts; AI cost per
 client

Inbox drafts stay on Claude Haiku 5.5. A plain rule in code picks the few
worth a second pass on Claude Sonnet 5.5: threads over 2,500 characters,
drafts with 2+ [GAP]s, or a repeat customer's question. Never urgent,
emergency, hand-off or Never email.

- Off per client until ticked on the admin levels card; 5 a day per
  client at most, on top of the normal daily cap.
- A failure, timeout or decline keeps Haiku's draft. Sonnet can only
  improve a draft or hand it to the owner, never loosen a rule.
- Structured output for the Sonnet call, since Sonnet 5.5 rejects the
  forced tool choice the Haiku call uses.
- Every model call logs tokens per client, day and model in D1
  (client_agent_tokens). Jerome's brief shows each client's AI cost this
  month at list prices.

New test_stepup.mjs (37 checks); all 9 suites and check_site.py pass.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
